model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "AppPages renders retained HTML with workerd's native parser and the shared portable URL, srcset and CSS rewrite policy. Attribute decoding uses the same pinned HTML parser dependency's decoder; decoding precedes URL rewriting and changed attributes escape ampersands before serialization. Native raw-text handling preserves the portable parser's bootstrap-marker behavior. Portable hosts retain their synchronous parser. AppPages supplies cryptography and path services only: remote assets and bound app runtimes require no local filesystem, process or terminal services. AppPages never reads an app's skills: its SDK skill source is a stub that dies, so the skill parser and its YAML reader stay out of the upload. Production upload checks reject the portable HTML engine, those local OS modules, the skill parser and YAML, and any uploaded module that calls the skills API. Cloud runtime API revisions read the shared API document directly, so AppPages does not retain the default application and management composition. Worker upload and startup budgets stay unchanged. Build aliases for workerd, parser and platform services apply only to app-pages; local test hooks remain shared and the OAuth wire mode keeps its protocol alias excluded."
    }
  }
}
